{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISION (AC1): DEPRECATE, not remove. Recorded with the evidence that decided it.\n\nWHY NOT OPTION 2 (remove now). Option 2's premise — that the key never changed behaviour in any shipped release where the port was already dormant — is FALSE. At shipped tag v0.10.1 the inbound probe was fully reachable (reconcile.py, apply_inbound.py, inbound_probe.py present and wired) and adapters/jira/probe.py::_resolve_resolved_statuses read jira.resolved_statuses to classify. The key was live and behaviour-affecting in a shipped release; it only became inert by v0.11.0 (the current version, released 2026-08-07), by which point bug 3b5f had already removed the consumers. On top of that, the pre-f020 docs actively told operators to set it: \"Set it if your self-hosted workflow names its resolved states differently — otherwise a resolved issue is misclassified.\" So real pyproject.toml files plausibly carry this key, and hard-removing it is a genuine upgrade hazard.\n\nWHY NOT OPTION 3 (keep for a future reader). ADR 0028 rules absence-vs-deletion discrimination OUTBOUND-owned, and the outbound path (outbound_differ._safe_get_issue + binding_walk) discriminates on HTTP status, not workflow status names. No concrete future consumer exists.\n\nWHY NOT HARD REMOVAL WITH A TOMBSTONE, i.e. the code_health.enabled precedent. That precedent (delete the field, add a warn-class tombstone so existing config still loads with a warning) is the right END state and is exactly what the follow-up ticket specifies. But it was applied \"per the operator ruling\" on bug a573-00ea-2bf6-4eb1 — sign-off came first. There is no such ruling here, and removing a documented operator-facing key is user-visible, so this ticket does the conservative half and defers the removal to an operator decision.\n\nWHAT WAS EXECUTED (AC2-AC4):\n- Both keys registered as _scheduled cfg retirements in _deprecations.py (replacement \"\", remove_in v1.0.0). They still parse and validate byte-identically; the only new behaviour is a warning.\n- coerce_sparse warns via a new _warn_deprecated_keys helper that looks the key up in _deprecations.REGISTRY directly. This adopts the plan-review's advisory finding (do not maintain a second parallel table). Extracting the helper also kept coerce_sparse under the C901 ceiling, which the inline loop had pushed from 15 to 16 — baselining that debt would have been the wrong trade.\n- _message now words an empty-replacement scheduled entry as a retirement (\"no longer has any effect\") rather than \"use <blank>\", mirroring the branch _tombstone_message already had.\n- The write-only DC plumbing is GONE: _TransportBase's resolved_statuses param and _resolved_statuses attribute, JiraDataCenterSettings.resolved_statuses, its resolution, DEFAULT_RESOLVED_STATUSES, and backend.py's ctor kwarg. Nothing read the value, so this is behaviour-neutral.\n- Because that removed the last read of ReconcilerConfig.resolved_statuses, BOTH schema fields now carry a `# read-via:` marker pointing at the follow-up f408-64ad-ee41-46b6; the heldout marker test now pins exactly two markers naming that ticket.\n- docs/config.md and docs/user-guide.md both describe the keys as deprecated, warning, scheduled for v1.0.0, removal tracked on f408. This also fixes the pre-existing inconsistency where user-guide.md attributed the f020/inert story to the reconciler key while the schema and config.md attributed it to the jira key.\n\nRECOMMENDATION carried to f408-64ad-ee41-46b6 (created, linked discovered_from): remove both keys via warn-class tombstones following the code_health.enabled precedent, once an operator signs off. Warn-class rather than error-class because neither key is operationally load-bearing — nothing breaks if it is ignored."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786560555282584001,"uuid":"d3826580-9670-4264-845f-4660e4c7385d"}